Closes #508.

Security hardening goals:
- cap configured trusted RPC proxy addresses at startup;
- bound trusted `X-Forwarded-For` hop count before allocating/walking the chain;
- preserve right-to-left trusted-proxy semantics, spoof resistance, direct-client behavior, and #288 fail-closed identity overflow;
- reuse one normalized trusted-proxy set on the production request path;
- add exact-bound, over-bound, invalid-hop, and config-cardinality regressions;
- document this as RPC pre-admission/DoS hardening only.

