## What changed

This PR restores the intended HOY menu product contract: the original restaurant menu is a source/provenance artifact, not the finished guest UI.

- adds a final `menu-native-standard-2.48.js` guest-menu authority after the existing source/integrity layers;
- only HOY-native structured menu items may be rendered as a finished guest menu;
- image-page, iframe/embed and external-source-only menus are stripped from the guest presentation and fail closed as `being prepared` until structured;
- menu locale is coupled to `state.lang`: DE page -> DE menu, EN page -> EN menu, ES page -> ES menu;
- switching language now reloads the matching translation catalog before re-rendering;
- a locale is shown only when every relevant structured item has a production-ready (`curated` / `operator_confirmed`) translation, including translated descriptions where source descriptions exist;
- incomplete locale coverage fails closed rather than mixing languages;
- menu chrome/search/status copy is localized for DE/EN/ES;
- PWA runtime wiring includes the final menu authority;
- regression tests now reject image/iframe menus as finished guest menus and verify DE -> EN -> ES locale coupling.

## Root cause

The previous pipeline had two product-contract breaks:

1. `image_complete` / `image_pages` and some embedded source states were allowed to count as a complete guest menu, so original image pages could appear as `Speisekarte in HOY`.
2. the later language-integrity layer loaded German translations only, while the page language button merely changed `state.lang` and re-rendered without loading the corresponding menu locale.

That allowed a technically green build to violate the intended consumer experience.

## Current data truth

Read-only Production inspection on 2026-08-19 shows:

- 2,078 active structured menu items across 32 restaurants;
- 902 `de / curated` translation rows;
- 5 restaurants currently have complete production-ready German coverage;
- 0 currently have complete English coverage;
- 0 currently have complete Spanish coverage;
- 8 full-menu sources are currently `image_complete` and therefore need structured import before they can become finished HOY menus.

This PR deliberately does **not** pretend that the missing data work is complete. EN/ES and image-only sources remain fail-closed until their structured, reviewed menu data exists.

## Buyer / product impact

This moves HOY back toward a consistent first-party structured menu product: searchable, filterable, language-aware, measurable and portable across restaurants and regions, rather than a collection of external/image menu presentations.

## Safety boundary

- no Supabase DDL/DML;
- no Production menu mutation;
- no deploy;
- no merge authorization;
- no external outreach;
- no claim that all DE/EN/ES menu data is already populated.

