## Purpose

Promote the Layer-1 nested authoring seam from issue #100 Pass 63 on current `main@376a0848670321dbafd36024e4570634c95cb021` after #140/#141.

This inverts canonical container expansion without crossing byte domains:

```text
child immutable payload
 -> child bounded writer
 -> authored child image
 -> exact materialized parent span
 -> alias arbitration
 -> parent WorkingCopy
 -> #140 parent layout writer
 -> validated parent authored image
```

## Exact parent/expansion binding

The reintegrator requires:

- readable immutable PAC/PNST parent with exact ResourceId size;
- usable exact `ContainerExpansion` for that parent;
- every populated child still byte-equal to its bounded parent span;
- child identity/source/offset binding to the supplied parent;
- exact authored child ResourceId match.

A stale expansion fails closed before edits.

## Authored child trust boundary

`AuthoredChildImage` carries exact child ResourceId, source/output SHA, revision, writer-mode identity and authored bytes. The reintegrator independently recomputes source/output SHA values.

For a **changed child classified as a container**, `writer_mode` is not trusted as proof. The reintegrator reconstructs a guarded verification WorkingCopy from the exact expanded child bytes, applies the authored same-size image, and independently runs canonical #140 `RelativeSlotLayoutWriter` again. A forged writer-mode string plus correctly recomputed SHA cannot hide structurally corrupted nested PAC/PNST bytes.

## Materialized-coordinate rule

All writes use `ContainerEntry.offset` inside the already-materialized parent image. The code never computes `compressed NBZ data offset + nested offset`.

Regression uses a parent with `zip_deflate` source provenance at offset `0x777` and proves the nested PNST is addressed only at materialized parent offset `0x20`.

## Duplicate-offset aliases

Populated children are grouped by exact parent `(offset,size)`:

- one changed alias -> patch shared span once;
- multiple byte-identical changed aliases -> patch once;
- divergent changed aliases -> fail closed `alias_conflict`;
- all alias identities remain visible in the receipt/topology.

## Parent validation

Each changed physical span becomes one guarded same-size parent WorkingCopy edit. The final parent is always passed through merged #140, so slot count, sparse/alias topology, offsets, bounded spans, total size and protected prefix remain unchanged.

No new `ByteProvenance` is invented; output remains authored bytes + authoring receipt until persistence/reopen.

## Regression

Covers:

- transformed parent / materialized child coordinate separation;
- two distinct PAC aliases sharing one PNST span;
- single-alias shared-span edit;
- identical dual-alias edit;
- divergent alias conflict;
- stale source/output SHA;
- forged writer mode + recomputed SHA + corrupted PNST magic -> independent child writer validation failure;
- size-changing authored image rejection;
- clean/no-change image;
- duplicate/unknown child input;
- stale parent/expansion;
- canonical parent reparse with duplicate-offset topology preserved.

## Boundary

Not included:

- runtime-synth size-changing nested rebuild;
- exact intrinsic child-size discovery;
- workspace parser-validation gate / FormatIntegrationRegistry correction;
- real legal nested-corpus authoring receipt;
- original-game execution receipt.

The already-merged #141 STORE-overlay writer consumes the resulting rebuilt **root** bytes after bottom-up propagation.

