## What changed

- added a read-only verifier for one controlled waitlist submission in the canonical Development Supabase project;
- derives deterministic consent and outbox identities from the controlled email and browser submission UUID;
- requires exactly one matching consent row and one matching outbox row;
- validates the full waitlist consent contract, exact evidence keys, canonical SHA-256 evidence checksum, outbox identity, provider correlation, and accepted/delivered state;
- rejects every Supabase project except Development before issuing a request;
- emits only a bounded summary with a masked email and short provider-reference fingerprint;
- added a CLI command, operator runbook, mocked query/contract tests, negative tests, and standard Supabase-validation wiring.

## Why

Issue #130 still requires real Development proof that a controlled browser submission persists the reviewed consent evidence, produces one durable delivery intent, stores the Resend provider message ID, and reaches accepted or delivered state without duplication. The existing implementation and unit tests do not provide a reusable, secret-safe way to validate that real database evidence.

## Safety

- GET-only Supabase queries;
- hard-coded canonical Development project guard;
- no Production access;
- no waitlist submission or email send;
- no consent/outbox mutation;
- no Resend webhook registration or invocation;
- no Vercel environment mutation;
- no secret, full provider message reference, message body, or authentication link in output;
- no customer data is required; the procedure requires a controlled non-customer alias.

## Operator command

From `apps/web`:

`npm run verify:waitlist-development`

Required values are supplied through a secure shell or approved secret runner and are never committed.

## Validation required

Fresh GitHub Web Quality and Vercel Preview must pass on the exact PR head before merge. This PR adds the verifier only; it does not activate the waitlist ledger or perform the controlled Development test.
